  "notes": "Six-count Weave from Promenade Position: one uninterrupted 1-2-3, 1-2-3 figure. Starts in the owner's existing feet-apart promenade (not a Whisk), closes during the opening two counts, passes outside partner on 4, and finishes in closed hold with feet apart, lead LF / follow RF weighted. A standalone figure; it does not require a Contra Check. Standard six-step order and footwork informed by https://www.ballroomdancers.com/dances/info.asp?sid=495 and https://ballroomguide.github.io/BallroomGuide/standard/waltz/weave_from_pp.html . Distances, compact turn distribution, rise and passing routes are provisional for subjective review, not an exact syllabus alignment chart. Only the first travelling steps intentionally cross in the body frame; dense tests cover every footprint and thigh/shin pair without omitting those intervals. All authoring, reach, lowering and balance checks run with unchanged limits. The open-foot closed-hold exit is not the catalogue's feet-collected closed stance; check joins when adding another figure."
